# Docs site UI

## Target

Clean documentation site (MDN-style). Readable typography, spacing, sidebar nav.

## Do

- CSS classes in `globals.css` — `.layout`, `.sidebar`, `.page`, `.prose`
- Wrap all page content in `.page` or `.prose`
- Server-rendered sidebar with section labels
- Subtle borders and spacing; muted text for secondary content

## Do not

- Card grids, hero sections, numbered badge circles
- Marketing CTAs ("Start reading", accent-color spans)
- Inline `style={}` in components
- `"use client"` for nav unless a tiny NavLink is truly needed
- Backdrop-blur, hover animation libraries, accent marketing colors

## Overcorrection warning

De-bloat ≠ remove all CSS. Unstyled HTML is as wrong as a SaaS landing page.
